## 4.1.1. Settings

mothraSettings = Corrector settings

## 4.1.1.1. Preset option

preset = Preset

preset-desc1 = Instead of configuring the mod manually, you can use ready-made setting groups called presets. The mod includes the following presets:
preset-desc2 = - Default: the most moderate preset of all. It is selected by default if the player hasn't changed the mod's settings.
preset-desc3 = - No mod: a preset that completely disables all mod changes. Useful for comparing the game before and after the mod's effects.
preset-desc4 = - Deflecat: the preset used by the mod's author, Deflecat. It reflects his personal preferences. It won't suit everyone!
preset-desc5 = If you prefer to configure everything yourself, don't be alarmed if a preset activates automatically during the process. This simply means you have selected the exact combination of options that corresponds to that preset. You can continue configuring the settings without issue.

## 4.1.1.1.1. Preset option variants

preset-default = Default
preset-vanilla = No mod
preset-deflecat = Deflecat

preset-none = None

## 4.1.1.2. Window title text category

opt-title-title = Window title text

opt-title-desc1 = You can choose the text displayed in the game window's title bar. Options:
opt-title-desc2 = - Original keeps everything exactly as it is in the base game.
opt-title-desc3 = - In Russian uses the Russian translation built into the mod.
opt-title-desc4 = - As in the field below uses the field below, where you can enter your own desired text.
opt-title-desc5 = The Default and Deflecat templates use the In Russian option. The No mod template uses the Original option.

